      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-97239",
      ":question/problem": "In a game, a player flips a coin and wins if the coin lands on heads. The coin is unfair, landing on heads once out of every $4$ tosses on average. Let $X$ represent the outcome of the game: $X = 1$ if the player wins and $X = 0$ if the player loses. By modeling the situation as a Bernoulli trial, determine the variance of $X$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
