      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-98084",
      ":question/problem": "To win a board game, Robert needs a $3$ or $4$ on the next roll of a fair die. Otherwise, he loses. Let $X$ represent the game's outcome: $X = 1$ if Robert wins and $X = 0$ if he loses. By modeling the situation as a Bernoulli trial, determine the standard deviation of $X$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
